we use linked-list to store obj in sequence.
but unlike arrays, linked-list can grow and shrink automatically.
we call the first node as "HEAD"
we call the last node as "TAIL"
each node store next node reference.
and we have two pointer on first and last node

Note: we have a head pointer on first node as head   (it's like git, git commits are linked_list)
      we have a tail pointer on last node as tail!
      but we can not use tail pointer to travers the list!
      the list is one direction.

Note: git commit as node of linked-list are immutable
      (we can not update the pointer!)
      but in general nodes are mutable in linked-list.

lookup by value is O(n)
                      we should travel from head to tail
                      to find a value

lookup by index  is O(n)
                      we should traverse the list again

Note: unlike Arrays where items are stored sequentially on RAM
      (that's because they are static, they need to fix)
      the Linked_list node can ba all over the place!
      (that's because they are dynamic)


INSERT

insert at the first          O(1)
                             create the new node
                             update the head to him

insert at the end is                   O(1)
                                          create the new node
                                          (we can find last node by tail)
                                          update the tail to him

insert at the middle                   O(n)
                                          find the appropriate node O(n)
                                          insert the node O(1)


DELETE

delete at the first       O(1)
                          update the head
                          remove the old pointer (IF WE DON'T REMOVE THE POINTER
                                                  GARBAGE COLLECTOR WILL NOT REMOVE THIS GARBAGE NODE!)

delete at the end         O(n)
                          travers to the end O(n)
                          update the tail
                          and remove the pointer from pre last node
                          (make pre last node as last node!)

delete at the end        O(n)
                         travers to the end O(n)


---------------------

LOOKUP --> O(n)

INSERT AT FIRST  --> O(1)
INSERT AT END    --> O(1)       //in services with huge insert, linked list is good!
INSERT AT middle --> O(n)

DELETE AT FIRST  --> O(1)
DELETE AT END    --> O(n)
DELETE AT middle --> O(n)

Note: middle is always O(n) due to traverse
      begin and end is always O(1)
      except delete the end, because we can not find the pre last item from tail
      we should traverse the list form him!
